WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.880
Welcome to Grade 5 English, Unit 9: Lights, Camera, Action…

2
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:12.740
Unit 9 is about scripts: the writing that actors
follow on a stage and in front of a camera.

3
00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:18.320
You will read “The Forest Guardians” first
as a play script and then as a film script,

4
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:24.420
comparing stage directions with camera
directions such as pan, zoom and close-up.

5
00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:29.940
You will also study compound nouns like
woodland, footpath and bamboo grove,

6
00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.920
and write and perform a short scene of your own.

7
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.040
The unit story, “Nookwatch: The Forest Mission”,

8
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:42.760
follows Amal and Sami as they help rescue
an injured lemur at a woodland rescue centre.

9
00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:48.300
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:54.490
By the end of this unit, you will be able to
recognise the layout and features of a play script,

11
00:00:54.890 --> 00:01:00.690
including the cast list, character names,
colons, dialogue and stage directions.

12
00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:05.410
You will also explain the difference
between a play script and a film script,

13
00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:09.830
using examples from both versions of “The Forest Guardians”.

14
00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:15.830
You will also read stage directions
accurately and locate upstage, downstage,

15
00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:19.510
centre stage and the entrances and exits they describe.

16
00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:22.310
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

17
00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:32.350
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: aggressive,
apparent, argument, abbreviation, simultaneously, ordinarily.

18
00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:38.350
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

19
00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:42.670
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

20
00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:49.330
The reading sequence includes The Forest
Guardians: a play script and The Forest Guardians:

21
00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:51.770
the same scene as a film script.

22
00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:53.350
Read actively.

23
00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:58.930
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

24
00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:03.630
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

25
00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:08.830
The first language focus is What a Compound Noun Is.

26
00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:15.150
A compound noun joins two or more words so
that together they name one single thing.

27
00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:20.530
Knowing the parts lets you work out a new word
without reaching for a dictionary every time.

28
00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:27.370
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

29
00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:33.430
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Read the Script Aloud.

30
00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:38.590
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

31
00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:42.630
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

32
00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:46.170
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

33
00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:47.810
You are ready to begin.

34
00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:54.570
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

35
00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:57.410
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

36
00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:05.030
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
